      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Relying on managed conservation as a primary strategy is increasingly outdated because it prioritizes human recreational and aesthetic needs over the intrinsic biological complexity of the ecosystem. This anthropocentric approach often results in habitat fragmentation and biodiversity loss by actively suppressing native species, mimicking undisturbed natural systems in a way that is neither natural nor sustainable. True ecological resilience is achieved only through rewilding, which allows self-organizing natural processes to restore missing species and functions, ultimately creating a more robust and independent environmental system.",
      "source": "target",
