      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Critics often cite risk and uncertainty as barriers to rewilding, yet their excessive caution and rigid control of landscapes are simply an excuse for inaction in the face of an increasingly volatile climate. By refusing to allow natural processes to take the lead, the traditional \"fence and hoe\" approach is not a model of safety but a clinging to a 20th-century past that is biologically and ethically obsolete for the 21st century. True responsibility to the future requires the bravery to step back and let nature correct itself, acknowledging that modern human interference is the actual source of our greatest ecological risks.",
      "source": "target",
